        <div class="card" style="padding: var(--spacing-xl);">
            <h3>1. What Are Cookies</h3>
            <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device to help websites function, remember preferences, and improve user experience.</p>
            <p>Cookies are tiny pieces of data that are downloaded and stored on your computer, tablet, or mobile device when you visit a website. They are widely used by websites to make them work more efficiently and to provide useful information to the website owners. Cookies can be either session cookies, which are temporary and deleted when you close your browser, or persistent cookies, which remain on your device for a specified period or until you manually delete them. First-party cookies are set by the website you are visiting, while third-party cookies are set by a domain other than the one you are visiting. NetSkill primarily uses first-party cookies for essential functionality, but we may also use limited third-party services that set their own cookies.</p>

            <h3>2. How We Use Cookies</h3>
            <p>NetSkill uses cookies and session data to keep you logged in, protect account security, store preferences, and analyze platform usage.</p>
            <p>Specifically, we use cookies for the following purposes. Authentication cookies allow us to remember that you are logged into your account so that you do not need to re-enter your credentials on every page you visit. Session management cookies keep track of your current browsing session and help maintain your progress as you navigate through courses. Security cookies help us detect and prevent fraudulent activity, protect your account from unauthorized access, and safeguard your personal information. Preference cookies remember your settings and preferences, such as your display preferences or previously selected filters, so that you have a more personalized experience each time you return to the platform. Analytics cookies collect anonymous information about how visitors use NetSkill, including which pages are visited most often, how long users spend on each page, and whether they encounter any errors. This data helps us continuously improve the platform and ensure that our content delivery is optimized for our users. Functionality cookies enable certain features of the platform, such as remembering your progress through a video tutorial or maintaining your course enrollment status across sessions.</p>

            <h3>3. Types of Cookies</h3>
            <p>We may use essential cookies (required for core functionality), preference cookies, and analytics-related cookies.</p>
            <p>Essential cookies are necessary for the platform to function correctly. They enable core features such as user login, session management, account security, and navigation. Without these cookies, certain parts of NetSkill may not function properly. Preference cookies allow the platform to remember choices you make, such as your preferred language, display settings, or course filter selections. These cookies provide a more convenient and personalized experience. Analytics cookies help us understand how users interact with our platform by collecting aggregated and anonymized usage data. We use this information to identify popular content, detect and fix performance issues, and make data-driven decisions about platform improvements. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies for marketing purposes, and we do not sell any browsing data to third-party advertisers.</p>

            <h3>4. Managing Cookies</h3>
            <p>You can control or delete cookies from your browser settings. Disabling essential cookies may affect platform functionality.</p>
            <p>Most web browsers allow you to control cookies through their settings preferences. You can typically choose to block all cookies, accept only first-party cookies, or be notified when a cookie is being set. Please note that if you choose to disable or reject cookies, certain features of NetSkill may become unavailable or may not function as intended. For example, you may not be able to stay logged in across page visits, and some interactive features may not work correctly. To manage cookies, you can adjust your browser settings. Instructions for popular browsers can usually be found in the help menu or settings section of your browser. For Google Chrome, you can go to Settings > Privacy and Security > Cookies and Other Site Data. For Mozilla Firefox, you can go to Options > Privacy & Security > Cookies and Site Data. For Safari, you can go to Preferences > Privacy. For Microsoft Edge, you can go to Settings > Site Permissions > Cookies and Site Data. You can also use your browser's incognito or private browsing mode, which automatically deletes session cookies when you close the browser window.</p>

            <h3>5. Third-Party Services</h3>
            <p>NetSkill may embed content from third-party services, such as YouTube for video tutorials. These services have their own cookie and privacy policies that are independent of ours. We encourage you to review the cookie policies of any third-party services we integrate. We do not control and are not responsible for the data collection practices of these third-party providers. Embedded YouTube videos may set cookies that track your viewing activity, but we have enabled privacy-enhanced mode where available to minimize data collection.</p>

            <h3>6. Updates to This Policy</h3>
